ablespoons of Italian seasoning\n- 1 egg\n- 16 ounces of ricotta cheese\n- 16 ounces of shredded mozzarella cheese\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n\nStep 1: Cook the Lasagna Noodles\nFill a large pot with salted water and bring it to a boil. Cook lasagna noodles for 8-10 minutes, or until they are al dente. Drain the water and set the noodles aside.\n\nStep 2: Make the Meat Filling\nIn a large skillet, cook the ground beef over medium heat. Add diced onions and garlic. Continue to cook until the onions are translucent and the meat is browned. Then, add tomato sauce, tomato paste, water, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper. Bring the mixture to a boil then reduce the heat and simmer for 20 minutes.\n\nStep 3: Mix The Cheese Filling\nIn a mixing bowl, combine ricotta cheese, 1 cup of shredded mozzarella cheese, and 1 beaten egg. Add salt and pepper to taste.\n\nStep 4: Preheat The Oven\nPreheat your oven to 375°F.\n\nStep 5: Assemble The Lasagna\nIn a large baking dish, spread a thin layer of meat sauce on the bottom. Layer lasagna noodles to cover the sauce, followed by a layer of cheese filling, and then a layer of meat sauce. Repeat these layers until all of the ingredients have been used. Top the final layer with remaining shredded mozzarella cheese.\n\nStep 6: Bake The Lasagna\nCover the baking dish with foil and bake in the oven for 25 minutes. Remove the foil and continue to bake for another 25 minutes, or until the top is golden brown.\n\nStep 7: Let the Lasagna Rest\nRemove the lasagna from the oven and let it rest for 10 minutes before serving. This helps the cheese and sauce settle and makes for easier cutting.\n\nSpecial Tips:\n\n- Add some fresh basil or oregano to the meat sauce mixture to elevate the flavor profile of the dish.\n- Consider boiling the lasagna noodles in salted chicken or beef broth rather than water to give the noodles more depth of flavor.\n- To make your lasagna more colorful and nutritious, add some spinach or kale to the cheese filling. Just be sure to squeeze out any excess water and finely chop the greens.\n- Consider using a mix of different meats - such as pork and beef - to make the dish more interesting.\n- If you like your lasagna saucier, just add more tomato sauce or keep some extra sauce on the","tokens":["<","|","im","_","start","|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","user","\n","Prov","ide"," a"," step","-","by","-","step"," guide"," on"," how"," to"," make"," your"," favorite"," type"," of"," las","agna",","," including"," the"," ingredients"," needed",","," the"," time"," required"," for"," each"," step",","," and"," the"," recommended"," oven"," temperature"," and"," baking"," duration","."," Additionally",","," describe"," any"," special"," techniques"," or"," tips"," for"," achieving"," the"," perfect"," flavor"," and"," texture",","," such"," as"," lay","ering"," the"," pasta"," with"," different"," types"," of"," sau","ces"," or"," adding"," specific"," herbs"," and"," spices"," to"," the"," meat"," filling",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","ass","istant","\n","Step","-","by","-","Step"," Guide"," to"," Making"," Classic"," Las","agna","\n","\n","In","g","redients",":","\n","-"," 1"," package"," of"," las","agna"," noodles","\n","-"," 1"," pound"," of"," ground"," beef","\n","-"," 1"," diced"," onion","\n","-"," 3"," cloves"," of"," minced"," garlic","\n","-"," 1"," jar"," of"," tomato"," sauce","\n","-"," 2"," tablespoons"," of"," tomato"," paste","\n","-"," 1"," cup"," of"," water","\n","-"," 2"," tablespoons"," of"," Italian"," season","ing","\n","-"," 1"," egg","\n","-"," 16"," ounces"," of"," ric","otta"," cheese","\n","-"," 16"," ounces"," of"," shredded"," mo","zz","are","lla"," cheese","\n","-"," Salt"," and"," pepper"," to"," taste","\n","\n","Step"," 1",":"," Cook"," the"," Las","agna"," N","ood","les","\n","Fill"," a"," large"," pot"," with"," salt","e